<!--Post: 7398--><!--Time: 1108463057-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7398"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Pax56<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Pax56<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 15, 2005 - 2:24 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->This thread is an offshoot of the &#34;Feedback On Messages  To/From BTK&#34;.  The alleged BTK poster refers to his &#34;novel thinking&#34;.  Numerous other aspects of the case touch on BTK&#39;s intelligence level - his writings, his planning, his poetry abilities - just to name a few.  Part of BTK&#39;s elusive nature appears to be connected to the fact that we aren&#39;t even positive how smart or how educated he really is. <BR> <BR>As a starting point, I&#39;m asking this question:  Is BTK capable of &#34;novel thinking&#34;?  By this I mean, is he capable of the kind of thinking we associate with researchers, inventors, artists, scientists, politicians &#40;good ones, at least&#41;, entrepreneurs, and others who come up with new ideas that change the world around them.  In particular, I&#39;m wondering if BTK could come up with novel criminal behaviors - new ways to battle law enforcement, not just minor variations on known criminal tactics.  If he is capable of such, then we may indeed need the same sort of &#34;novel thinking&#34; to bring him to justice.  But any aspect of BTK&#39;s intelligence is relevant to this thread.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7398-->
<!--Post: 7411--><!--Time: 1108482191-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7411"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 15, 2005 - 7:43 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->&#34;Psychologist worked BTK case in late 1970’s&#34; <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.ksn.com/news/stories/6974024.html" target=_top>http://www.ksn.com/news/stories/6974024.html</a> <BR> <BR>I absolutly belive that BTK´s IQ is above average, actually quite a bit. <BR> <BR>I´ll be back on this subject supporting my opinion above. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7411-->
<!--Post: 7413--><!--Time: 1108486312-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7413"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:hkenley@san.rr.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Chiefron<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Chiefron<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 15, 2005 - 8:51 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Pax56, <BR> <BR>From you list of three things that touch on BTK&#39;s intelligence level, you can strike both his poetry abilities and his writing, if you are convinced he is intelligent. Using standard grading criteria and several different automated grammar parsing programs, I have concluded that BTK had about an 8th grade education level. And that is being generous. Most of his writing falls in the 3rd to 4th grade level. Adding proper punctuation to his lowest writings only raises it to the 8th grade level.  <BR> <BR>Obviously I realize that writing level is not a direct reflection of IQ, however I have yet to meet someone with genius level IQ who could force themselves to write so poorly. <BR> <BR>You have to believe the &#34;He is so smart that he wants us to think he is dumb&#34; theory to justify it. The problem with that is, it is a self contradicting theory. He is so self absorbed that he wants the police to know he is smarter than they are and they cannot catch him. In order to do this he writes in a childish manner so that we think he is dumber than he really is. I think the illogic of that is fairly apparent. <BR> <BR>Ron<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7413-->
<!--Post: 7420--><!--Time: 1108490321-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7420"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Iq<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Iq<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 15, 2005 - 9:58 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Chief,  <BR> <BR>I believe BTK is highly intelligent and the spelling and grammar errors were very effective in allowing him to convey his message without revealing anything about himself. BTK knew that he would be writing many communications to media and LE and he also knew that experts would be examining every word of these communications. This much writing can reveal speach patterns, ethnicity, age, cultural background, social status, and much more. <BR> <BR>It&#39;s obvious that the way the letters are written is not the way that he communicates, listen to the 911 call. I am not saying he is a genius, or even that he attended college. I&#39;m saying he thinks that he is smart, and he&#39;s right. He has above average knowledge in all of the following areas: <BR> <BR>Law enforcement procedures <BR>Surveillance tactics <BR>Human Psychology <BR>Print and Television media <BR>Military prisoner interrogation <BR>Photography <BR> <BR>In addition, I belive he has demonstrated that he is/was a working class individual. People around him DO NOT know how smart he really is and he has always used this to his advantage.  <BR> <BR>It may sound like I&#39;m a wannabe profiler but I assure you, that&#39;s not the case. I&#39;ve just followed this for quite a while and kept notes. Even though my beliefs are all based on the facts of the case and the actual communications, they are still ONLY MY OPINIONS. <BR> <BR>I just want you to understand WHY I believe BTK is smart. Hope you don&#39;t take offense. <BR> <BR>iq<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7420-->
<!--Post: 7422--><!--Time: 1108491285-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7422"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Angrywolf<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Angrywolf<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 15, 2005 - 10:14 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I agree that BTK is above average intelligence..I wince when people on other boards say he isn&#39;t very bright.........I think they&#39;re just making self-serving statements.....trying to &#34;match wits&#34; <BR>with him by offering their off the wall theories about him...Unless he makes a mistake or the police get&#34;lucky&#34; I DON&#39;T SEE THEM EVER CATCHING HIM.....I have proposed setting a &#39;trap&#39; to catch him but Tom Voight and the others quickly shot it down and persist in their theories that if the police release more info he will be caught...but the police show no sign of doing that...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7422-->
<!--Post: 7423--><!--Time: 1108491416-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7423"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 15, 2005 - 10:16 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Question: <BR> <BR>Could BTK use one of those parsing apps to &#34;dumb down&#34; his letters and/or poetry?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7423-->
<!--Post: 7424--><!--Time: 1108492326-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7424"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->X3maine<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->X3maine<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 15, 2005 - 10:32 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->when i was in school, i used to get in trouble, not pay attention, daydream, and get miserable grades. <BR> <BR>in 7th and 8th grades, we took something called the Iowa Tests &#40;standardization tests&#41;. I always scored in the 99th percentile, which none of the other kids could believe because they thought i was a moron. <BR> <BR>the point is, just because someone acts and appears a certain way, that is no surefire indication of how that individual actually is. <BR> <BR>in 7th gade, my reading/writing levels were college level. however, you could look at a lot of things i had written and thought i was a coffee mug! the same pattern exists with me today. <BR> <BR>conversely, just because someone is college educated, with a masters or doctorate, does not mean that person is intelligent. i have seen many of these &#34;learned&#34; people who are dumb as a fistful of kangaroos...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7424-->
<!--Post: 7428--><!--Time: 1108493600-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7428"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Joel<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Joel<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 15, 2005 - 10:53 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->IMO BTK possesses above-average intelligence and is probably educated to college level. He&#39;s not the genius level he perhaps believes he is, but he is smart. AS Iq posts above he certainly has strong knowledge of a number of fields. <BR> <BR>His poorly spelt and composed communications are a blind to obfuscate this intelligence and conceal information about himself. The &#39;Is English not BTK&#39;s First Language&#39; thread has a great post with a English as a foreign language teacher examining his letters which is pretty persuasive. <BR> <BR>Bmodule - I don&#39;t believe BTK would need &#39;parsing apps&#39; &#40;i&#39;m assuming that&#39;s computer aid&#41; to alter his communications, although it&#39;s possible. <BR> <BR>It is feasable he&#39;s dyslexic or has a similar condition, but in this case I don&#39;t think that&#39;s true.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7428-->
<!--Post: 7429--><!--Time: 1108493774-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7429"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Topsailgrl<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Topsailgrl<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 15, 2005 - 10:56 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thank you X3maine! That explanation is it in a nutshell! You can have a masters degree and have trouble tying your own shoes! <BR> <BR>While BTK is more than likely of above average intelligence, I highly doubt he is of extraordinary intelligence. He is more cunning, calculating, and manipulative than of a higher IQ level. He is much more intelligent than his known writings lead us to believe, but reveals himself in the thought process of his writings as being above average in intelligence,hence a ruse.  <BR> <BR>I think BTK believes himself to be of a higher intelligence but his emotional side gets in the way. I don&#39;t mean emotions in the way a &#34;normal&#34; functioning person feels them. I mean in the narcissistic, psychopathic way. For instance, I believe that he did not plan on reemerging at the time he did. I think that the announcement that Robert Beattie would dare to write a book about him thinking him dead infuriated him. He wanted to one up the media and LE one more time with the most fantastical of all serial killers by writing his own story to be revealed either at the time of his death or some other time of his choosing and his emotions got in the way of this diabolical plan.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7429-->
<!--Post: 7434--><!--Time: 1108495601-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7434"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 15, 2005 - 11:26 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think that the theorie  <BR> <BR>&#34;He is so smart that he wants us to think he is dumb&#34;  <BR> <BR>should read like this: <BR> <BR>&#34;his writing skills/style is  talented/intelligent, and also known to many people, but he is smart enough to &#34;hide&#34; behind a lower educated way of writing&#34; <BR> <BR>Even if this is what he does I feel that a special kind of sophistication is still there to bee &#34;seen&#34;.  <BR>It is his starnge way of beeing able to be evil in a polite way, yes I know it sounds weird neither the less, that is my opinion. <BR> <BR>Also his ability to present himself as a victim of &#34;the monster&#34; despite he IS the monster while writing about it. <BR> <BR>There is a duality in all his writing wich IMO require a person of high intelligence. That said his emotional intelligence is, no daubt, almost non exsitence. <BR> <BR>His abilty of &#34;novel thinking&#34; IMO is absolutly present. He shows it in his skills in &#34;manegeing the evil crime circus&#34; in a way that is so different from other criminals. Think of that a whole policedepartment, FBI, profilers ect ect ect haven´t been able to catch him in a period of 30 years and that even if he has delivered an HUGE amount of communication, crimescenes, DNA ect ect to study. That IS Novel Thinking IMO, though a very destructive way of using the talent.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7434-->
<!--Post: 7437--><!--Time: 1108495999-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7437"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Steve_huff<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Steve_huff<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 15, 2005 - 11:33 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I honestly think IQ is an overrated method of estimating a person&#39;s capabilities, and applies very little to questions of why and how serial killers do things. <BR> <BR>If my accomplishments and abilities matched my IQ, I&#39;d be a wealthy physicist right now, and I most assuredly am NOT.  <BR> <BR>That said, BTK&#39;s probably above-average but not genius - capable in his chosen profession, most likely, and probably good with math, engineering, with his hands. He&#39;s not as literarily astute as he probably thinks. I&#39;d imagine it&#39;s true that he has a phenomenal memory, but memory and the ability to synthesize and hypothesize from what one remembers are two different things. There are autistics that appear to have total recall, but they are more like machines regurgitating narrative of events without analysis - while amazing memories are interesting, they aren&#39;t markers of great intellect, necessarily. <BR> <BR>BTK is shrewd, I think, in an animal way. Somewhere I&#39;ve seen someone use an analogy to an animal, like the coelocanth or the mountain gorilla. People don&#39;t think this animal exists, upon hearing tales. Then one day, after years and years of teams of searchers hunting the animal, they come upon it&#39;s territory, and even then only after considerable patience do they spot the creature.  <BR> <BR>The ability to camouflage one&#39;s self is not an indicator of great IQ - it&#39;s an indicator of animal cunning, which is linked to a different area of the brain and psyche altogether. <BR> <BR>I think the key may be in understanding that BTK, while murderous, is not a complete psychopath. Whatever vestiges of conscience he has in comparison to other killers has saved him. Killers are caught because they are often psychopaths, and in their arrogance they slip up. Something has kept BTK&#39;s antisocial arrogance in check just enough to never let him get too cocky.  <BR> <BR>I do not mean that I think he feels bad about what he&#39;s done. I do think he&#39;s intensely aware of just how serious his crimes were, and he&#39;s managed, probably through a great deal of almost obsessive thought about it, to constantly keep this in the front of his mind. He never forgets just how badly law enforcement wants him, never takes it for granted. An antisocial or psychopathic personality, one with no conscience of any sort, almost always forgets this in their pursuit of what they want, which is the bottom line for these animals.  <BR> <BR>IQ in the sense of how well this killer did in school, perhaps, is not a crucial thing to consider in my mind where BTK is concerned. His shrewdness and knowledge of police techniques, methods, this is much more pertinent, to me.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7437-->
<!--Post: 7438--><!--Time: 1108496578-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7438"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Steve_huff<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Steve_huff<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 15, 2005 - 11:42 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;d add to what chiefron says about the poetry abilities.  <BR> <BR>Take it from a legitimately &#40;not self&#41; published poet - BTK has NO poetic ability.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7438-->
<!--Post: 7440--><!--Time: 1108498627-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7440"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Iq<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Iq<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 15, 2005 - 12:17 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Very good Steve! <BR> <BR>You got the point across very well and I agree.  <BR> <BR>So here&#39;s a question for everyone to ponder:  <BR> <BR>Do you think that BTK has been able to elude being identified and captured because of his intellect? <BR> <BR>Or, do you think his  <BR> <BR>iq<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7440-->
<!--Post: 7451--><!--Time: 1108502689-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7451"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Joel<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Joel<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 15, 2005 - 1:24 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I agree that BTK shows a high degree of cunning, criminal methods and intuition which aren&#39;t related to IQ or other benchmark&#39;s of intelligence. <BR> <BR>His intellect &#40;above-average&#41; certainly would aid these traits in the commission of his crimes. His murders are more likely to have been unsolved due to his experience in lower-level crimes &#40;breaking entering, peeping and other voyeuristic activities&#41; and his familiarity with their successful commission than his IQ. <BR> <BR>My personal opionion is that he committed burglaries and was an active voyeur before committing his first murder. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7451-->
<!--Post: 7454--><!--Time: 1108503296-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7454"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:linnieskid@earthlink.net" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Linnieskid<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Linnieskid<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 15, 2005 - 1:34 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Joel, couldn&#39;t agree more. Some serial killers do <BR>have above average to high level I.Q.&#39;s but look at Otis Toole et. al.  Literally &#39;dumb $hits&#39;with little or no education. They got by with murders for so long by being comfortable with peeping and buglaries &#40;lots of practice&#41;  and graduated to murder along with their level of comfort.  Many of these people had just plain ol &#34;dumb luck&#34; and probably a high level of intuition, as you so astutley stated.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7454-->
<!--Post: 7465--><!--Time: 1108508482-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7465"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Elsbarn<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Elsbarn<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 15, 2005 - 3:01 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think BTK has average intelligence &#40;and would say good visual memory and spatial ability due to his descriptions of the crime scenes but it appears he used photographs&#41;. BTK may have compensated for his other processing weaknesses &#40;such as lack of organizational ability, planning and other exectutive functions&#41; and it would not surprise me if he had spent much time working out written lists, diagrams and plans before he made a hit, meaning it wasn&#39;t just some effortless ability that he has to avoid detection. <BR> <BR>His verbal skills are adequate to function in life--BUT, he is an overall poor writer and typist. I may be in the small group that does not believe he faked the mistakes to throw the police off. Nevertheless, the guy wanted to be a poet. Plenty have blasted his style but he does use poetic elements that indicate some training in the area, like the sort of training you might get in a lower level poetry course &#40;simile, metaphor, alliteration, repeated verses, and so on&#41;.  The &#34;Poetic Strangler&#34; could more aptly be the &#34;Poetry Strangler&#34; in the end though. <BR> <BR>I am not sure that there is a true processing strength evidenced in BTK&#39;s behavior and writings, but since we don’t have his IQ test here to analyze, it is not possible to know for sure. He is good with knots apparently but, then again, he has a high motivation to be good with knots--this would pertain to all the other elements that iq mentioned in the 4th post above. <BR> <BR>Back to the original question: is BTK capable of novel thinking? I think so. It may not be the sort that will win him any professional accolades, but he has demonstrated some skills, like Joel says, that place him in a diffent plane than the average criminal. How many think it&#39;s cute to leave messages for the police in cereal boxes? His personality disorder, however, skews any ability that he may have so that most of us cannot &#40;without study&#41; understand his thinking processes.  <BR> <BR>I also agree with Joel that he was a voyeur prior to committing his first murder. No way did he hatch from fantasy to full fledge serial killer without testing the waters first.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7465-->
<!--Post: 7471--><!--Time: 1108510501-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7471"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:nugzter@yahoo.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Nugzter<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nugzter<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 15, 2005 - 3:35 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Is it possible that BTK uses misspelling and gramatical errors because it keeps LE from IDing any writing patterns. Except his on purpose mistakes. Writing pattens and forgery analasys has been used for ages. He would have known this if he is as intellegent as we all think.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7471-->
<!--Post: 7487--><!--Time: 1108516493-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7487"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Iceteajan<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Iceteajan<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 15, 2005 - 5:14 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The one thing that I see missing from our intelligence assessment is the TIME FACTOR. <BR> <BR>I believe if you give somebody enough time, they can probably master any devious plan, and cover their tracks effectively. <BR> <BR>BTK probably has had a lot of time on his hands to fantasize and develop a &#34;perfect&#34; crime. <BR> <BR>Oh sure, he got surprised here and there, but he still weaseled out of the situation.  <BR> <BR>Not necessarily a reflection of IQ; it is reflection of imagination, planning, sheer nerve, and possibly a back-up plan.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7487-->
<!--Post: 7494--><!--Time: 1108520005-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7494"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 15, 2005 - 6:13 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Using the Intelligence Quotient&#40;IQ&#41; to determine an individual&#39;s level of intelligence is unsatisfactory. IQ examinations measure the ability of a candidate to analyze simple problems and determine patterns in phrases and puzzles. An IQ examination does not assess an individual&#39;s capacity to craft a composition or their ability to sustain an argument or rigorously investigate their logic. <BR> <BR>The BTK strangler seems to possess a high level of intelligence. It does not imply he held a Rhodes scholarship or a Fulbright scholarship. I suspect he attended and graduated from Wichita University. His undergraduate education would have concentrated on the physical sciences or engineering. His ability in the humanities may be less impressive. His ability to write poetry does not rival Yeats or Tennyson. His writing style does not reflect his grammar. The writing style attempts to conceal his level of education, ethnicity, class and age. <BR> <BR>The BTK Strangler&#39;s level of intelligence cannot be adequately explained by the level of his IQ or academic achievement. Cunning and instinct are important qualities implemented by the unknown subject. It has assisted him in planning the murders, taunting the police and public and avoiding apprehension. The unknown subject&#39;s understanding of photography, the electronic media, law enforcement and psychology are significant predictors of his intelligence.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7494-->
<!--Post: 7506--><!--Time: 1108529855-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7506"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:williammichael@direcway.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Oklahoma_mike<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Oklahoma_mike<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 15, 2005 - 8:57 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Perhaps in this discussion it would be helpful to discuss what is actually meant by &#39;intelligence quotient&#39;.  I know some of the posters know it well, but some may not.  So, in a nutshell: <BR>GOOD IQ tests &#40;and there are some&#41; are created by using a group of individual tests measuring different skills.  Thse include both verbal and nonverbal skills.  The lists of questions and activities in each sub-test is given to a sample, as large as possible, and as closely as possible representing the population as a group &#40;so many of each racial group, education level, part of the country, etc.&#41;  When all this data is colelcted, the average scores of the entire group becomes the average intelligence.  This is assigned a point value of 100, with the proportions abvove and below plotted on a graph.  Different tests use different graphs, so the same person may well score slightly different on 2 different tests and actually be at the same level. <BR>Since no test is totally accurate, the scores are looked at in a range.  As the tests vary, there is some difference, but all are close to this example:  below 70-the politically incorrect but accurate term retarded; 70-85 borderline &#40;Forrest Gump is an example here&#41;; 85-95 dull normal; 95-110, average &#40;or normal&#41;; 110-120 bright normal; 120-140, talented and/or gifted.  Above 140, genius. <BR>The best tests also give both a verbal and a non-verbal IQ.  In most people these are close together, but not exactly the same.  If there is a lot of difference one suspects something is wrong.  For example, a non-verbal of 120 but a verbal of 90 would hint at dyslexia or something similar. <BR>About 50% of everybody falls in the average, about 25% above and 25% below.  Only about 2-3% of people are below 70 or above 140. <BR>I estimate btk to be in the bright normal range, maybe between 115 and 120.  I suspect his non-verbal score is higher than his verbal but not a lot, maybe 10 points or so.  I also see aspects of novel thinking and creativity in btk consistent with some artistic ability.  Many artists tend to score in the bright normal range. <BR>Overall, I will hazard a guess that btk is one of the rarest of individuals, a right-brained engineer! &#40;almost all engineer types are left-brained&#41;. <BR>and that is far too much psych 101 for me!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7506-->
<!--Post: 7507--><!--Time: 1108531132-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7507"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 15, 2005 - 9:18 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Steve, that&#39;s the best post I&#39;ve seen regarding BTK&#39;s skills and mental acumen. To one of the things you posited, <i>BTK is shrewd, I think, in an animal way,</i> I&#39;ll add a powerful intangible: patience. I believe BTK has patience to burn and that patience, as much as anything else, has helped BTK remain uncaptured. <BR> <BR>I remember a tape recording. Sixteen or seventeen years ago, when asked his perception of the &#40;then&#41; at-large Green River Killer, a voice says, &#34;He may not be highly analytical but <i>he knows his stuff. He knows his stuff the way a fox knows his stuff.&#34;</i> -- Ted Bundy. <BR> <BR>I&#39;m not comparing Ridgeway and BTK. Salient point, to me, is the italicized portion of Bundy&#39;s quote.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7507-->
<!--Post: 7516--><!--Time: 1108536932-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7516"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Pax56<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Pax56<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 15, 2005 - 10:55 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Wow!  I really appreciate the thought and insight all of you folks have put into these responses.  Frankly, I&#39;m overwhelmed.  This is really helping me to pin down his abilities.  More proof of the power of the internet.  It&#39;s like seeing him from over a dozen different vantage points, when he hoped he would be invisible.  And while it&#39;s a tough act to follow, it&#39;s not too late for others to post - dare I say it, keep &#39;em coming!  -pax<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7516-->
<!--Post: 7519--><!--Time: 1108545708-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7519"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 16, 2005 - 1:21 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Pax, <BR>This is one of the best threads I&#39;ve read; the number of responses surprises me not one jot. <BR> <BR>I neglected to mention that I do believe BTK is capable of novel thinking per your definition. I used the word intangible earlier and repeat it here. BTK strikes me as one of those people who,  without any training or practice, takes apart and fixes the motor of a broken-down lawnmower with comparative ease. One of those types who &#34;just seems to know what to do.&#34; Not at every occasion, not by a long shot. But BTK seems to have an innate sense of awareness which is difficult to describe. He&#39;s not gifted, but significantly above average as to intelligence. Top fifteen percent, but much closer to eighty-five percent than one hundred. &#40;Or would it be 99?&#41;.  <BR> <BR>Can one really test an imagination? I say, no. To be sure, imagination can be measured <i>to a degree</i> by a variety of means, including simple observation. But at some point, it becomes an exercise in futility. I&#39;m trying to work all of this into something that might be used to pursue BTK, but am not succeeding. I&#39;ll give it a little time and see if anything comes to me. <BR> <BR>A word about luck. It does seem a little disrespectful to the victims - and in general - to opine that BTK is noticably intelligent. &#40;&#34;He&#39;s not intelligent, he was lucky!&#34;&#41; I  believe BTK has had a considerable run of good luck. But the intelligence - and the intangibles - is also there, in my opinion.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7519-->
<!--Post: 7562--><!--Time: 1108579380-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7562"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:hkenley@san.rr.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Chiefron<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Chiefron<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 16, 2005 - 10:43 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I may not have made myself clear in my post. I believe that BTK is smart. But I think it is in very specific things. He is organized, but organized like someone who learned to be organized after his formative years. I am this way. Was very disorganized as a youth, but was forced to learn organizational skills and attention to detail as an adult in the military and that forced behavior shows. I think Steve hit it just right when he said he had animal cunning. BTK need not be overly bright to learn most of the skills except psychology that IQ attributes to him. Just like a dog is not a genius level thinker but can be trained to some amazing things. In my opinion his understanding of human psychology is pretty limited anyway. <BR> <BR>My post focused primarily on the idea that BTK dumbs down his writing to make us think he is dumb. BTK could be completely illiterate and still have considerable ability in other areas.  <BR> <BR>Ron<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7562-->
<!--Post: 7599--><!--Time: 1108593892-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7599"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Angrywolf<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Angrywolf<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 16, 2005 - 2:44 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Oh boy..now he&#39;s cunning,etc etc...more tap dancing around the issue...btk is very intelligent according to any standard...anyway...unless he is caught we&#39;ll never know how smart he really is...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7599-->
<!--Post: 7616--><!--Time: 1108604277-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7616"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Audreyamw<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Audreyamw<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 16, 2005 - 5:37 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->For resource purposes here are some links to sites with info on IQ and intelligence measurement: <BR> <BR><a href="http://members.shaw.ca/delajara/IQBasics.html" target=_top>http://members.shaw.ca/delajara/IQBasics.html</a> <BR><a href="http://library.thinkquest.org/C005704/content_la_intel_measuring.php3" target=_top>http://library.thinkquest.org/C005704/content_la_i ntel_measuring.php3</a> <BR> <BR>IQ averages for various occupations:  <a href="http://members.shaw.ca/delajara/Occupations.html" target=_top>http://members.shaw.ca/delajara/Occupations.html</a> <BR> <BR>Also a basic IQ scale: <BR> <BR>IQ Range  	 <BR> <BR>Classification <BR>140 and over -- Genius or near genius <BR>120-140 -- Very superior intelligence <BR>110-120 -- Superior intelligence <BR>90-110 -- Normal or average intelligence <BR>80-90 -- Dullness <BR>70-80 -- Borderline deficiency <BR>Below 70 -- Definite feeble-mindedness <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7616-->
<!--Post: 7617--><!--Time: 1108605053-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7617"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Audreyamw<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Audreyamw<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 16, 2005 - 5:50 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->This is a really interesting thread.  Great brainwave, Pax56. <BR> <BR>I think BTK definitely has an IQ above 130.  He seems to be self-taught in many areas &#40;writing poetry, police methods, the obvious SK activities&#41;, which to me indicates a breadth of curiousity about the world, and better still he has a memory like a steel trap -- he retains whatever he learns. He has solid powers of concentration and organization. He apparently can draw well and in a lot of precise detail. He has strong reasoning skills. <BR> <BR>But what&#39;s interesting to me is how the fact that he&#39;s a psychopath would have an impact on his reasoning abilities.  Whatever raw intelligence he has would be shaped by a lack of conscience, a lack of emotional empathy, a need for strong stimulation, and also his sadistic tendencies.  He would be &#40;mis&#41;perceiving information about the world around him through this perspective. <BR> <BR>As a result, he produces things like the strange poetry.  I read somewhere that psychopaths can mimic ordinary emotions without feeling them, kind of like &#34;knowing the notes but not the tune&#34; -- that&#39;s the perfect description of his poetry. <BR> <BR>BTK has above-average intelligence.  But he also has plenty of intellectual blindspots too, due to the psychopathy, IMHO.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7617-->
<!--Post: 7674--><!--Time: 1108652288-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7674"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Surfietx<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Surfietx<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 17, 2005 - 6:58 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Just a quick thought, but could the &#34;novel&#34; thinking be a reference to his chapters, i.e. novel?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7674-->
<!--Post: 7835--><!--Time: 1108705880-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7835"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Angrywolf<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Angrywolf<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 17, 2005 - 9:51 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->MSN had an IQ test which I took..it said my IQ was 160..soI guess that makes me BTK right ? I still believe BTK has above average intelligence...he&#39;s playing a game..a role playing game..I play those..usually you want to rule the world or save the world at the end...I don&#39;t know what BTK&#39;s objective is..but he&#39;s is playing a serial killer acting out a fantasy and he can be as bizarre as he wants to . It&#39;s his game.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7835-->
<!--Post: 8174--><!--Time: 1108954638-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8174"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Seesthru<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Seesthru<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->9-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 20, 2005 - 6:57 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->BTK fancies himself a wordster in more ways than one, but he is far from talented. He sees his writings as works of art, and as clever taunts, but in fact they are embarrasingly  stilted and childish.  That is no indication of intelligence or lack thereof, it&#39;s just what is.  I believe he is slightly above average intelligence, but he&#39;s no Einstein.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8174-->
<!--Post: 8175--><!--Time: 1108954841-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8175"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Seesthru<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Seesthru<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->9-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 20, 2005 - 7:00 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Angrywolf, the computer IQ tests are no real indicator of IQ.  I took  them, and always scored much higher that in &#34;real&#34;  life.   The test a psych doc would give you is much different, and covers many more aspects.  I had a 139 in lingual ability, however  scored a mere 108 in spatial ability, in the &#34;real life&#34;  tests.  On the computer tests, I scored anywhere from a 98 to a 176.  I know I&#39;m no Einstein, so   I dont&#39; rely on the computer online tests as anythign more than amusement.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8175-->
<!--Post: 8204--><!--Time: 1108981717-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8204"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 21, 2005 - 2:28 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->No matter what they say, IQ tests are biased, demand subjective interpretation and are often astonishingly misleading. As a society, we enjoy &#34;testing&#34; people and we enjoy even more placing people in categories. Note the clear-cut definitions of IQ scores. Then we have Rorschach tests, which are more than half a century old. These tests are great for aiding in diagnosing psychosis but that&#39;s about all. Read &#34;House Of Cards&#34; if you want the low-down on the psychology raket.  <BR> <BR>Consider two Freudianesque remarks, &#34;By picking his nose in spite of all commands to the contrary, or when a youth is all the time sticking his finger through his buttonhole...the analytic teacher knows that the appetite of the lustful one knows no limits in his phantasies&#34; &#40;Quoted by Prof C. from Dr. Oskar Pfister, <i>The Psychoanalytical method,&#34; 1917, NY., p 79.</i> or <i>The little cap of red velvet in the German version of Little Red Riding Hood is a symbol of menstruation.</i> &#40;Quoted by Prof C. from Erich Fromm, <i>The Forgotten Language</i>, 1951 NY., p.240&#41;. What next? Person-Tree-House drawings? Did you know that when the lobotomy was first used it was considered painless? No anesthesia was given. Did you know that Insulin Shock was considered a major breakthrough for a good stretch of years? Sorry, but I become a little cautious when the psychobabble starts to really kick-in full-throttle. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8204-->
<!--Post: 8237--><!--Time: 1109011451-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8237"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Maxgravis<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Maxgravis<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 21, 2005 - 10:44 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Here is my 2 cents worth, He has to be pretty smart somewhat, he has out smarted LE for 30 years. Or he is extremely lucky, and if he is, he should by a lottery ticket!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8237-->
<!--Post: 8584--><!--Time: 1109213000-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8584"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Elsbarn<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Elsbarn<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 23, 2005 - 6:43 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Someone over at the Eagle boards has posted as BTK and writes about his intelligence. The post is: <BR> <BR><i>Once again, disbelief has set in. Rumors run rampant through the threads and some members make threats, others fake psychic revelations, some of you attempt to shmooze up to me. How gullible and naive do you think I must be? I am not the average Joe &#40;had to throw that in&#41;. I am highly intelligent with an IQ double what most of you seem to have. The game is no longer fun here, as it is at amateur level. I have disclosed clues, hints and private details that only I &#40;BTK&#41; would know. You choose to discredit me and say, &#39;no no, he&#39;s a fake BTK&#39;. You don&#39;t want to hear and read about the ghoulish details of my crimes and what ticks in my mind. You like your safe havens, at home behind your computers and under your blankets. <BR> <BR>I am not saying what I do and have done is not wrong, I don&#39;t even attempt to justify it, only explain the reasoning in my mind. It has become a game to me, in my mind, with the media and WPD, as well as, you amateur sleuths. It is like a game of clue with endless suspects. You have the clues, the where, the how, now all you need is BTK. If you would have looked in Maui, HI. in February of 2004, you would have found me, but only for a week. <BR> <BR>This will be my last posting, my last response with you simple minded degenerates. You&#39;re almost as bad as the lazy, worthless welfare recipients who choose not to work and make taxpayers feed their illiterate offspring. Society today is pathetic! <BR> <BR>Please continue on with your rambling theories and your assinine assumptions, it makes for a good laugh. I often think of various configurations you concoct while out on the greens. Somehow though, hitting that ball is not quite the same as hitting the Otero&#39;s. The latter gave me complete satisfaction. The thrill of the kill shall we say. I often wonder what was going through Julie&#39;s mind when I let her have her life back only to take it away again. <BR> <BR>Just so you all know, I removed my previous posts, not AMW. As I will with this post, it will be deleted and disappear into the shadows with me, lurking, watching and waiting for my next victim&#40;s&#41;. Will it be you? Your daughter? Maybe your mother or grandmother? Rest assured, it will be someone and you will all know it was at the hands of BTK! <BR> <BR>Goodbye my friends <BR> <BR>Chills &amp; Shivers one last time, <BR> <BR>The one and only BTK </i> <BR> <BR>Who knows who this character is, but in the scenario where a &#34;ghoulish&#34; BTK has actually gone around posting, then threads like this may have hit home and have cost tax payers nothing. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8584-->
<!--Post: 8586--><!--Time: 1109215637-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8586"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 23, 2005 - 7:27 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Elsbarn, I think you may be off topic of the &#39;BTK Intellegence Level&#39; thread. For more on that poster go over to the &#39;Communications&#39; page and then on to the &#39;BTK is posting on AMW&#39; thread that Skov started. So apparently this poster that you have quoted from the Eagle board is the same one who is posting on the America&#39;s Most Wanted board. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8586-->
<!--Post: 8627--><!--Time: 1109254560-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8627"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:embersageblue@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 24, 2005 - 6:16 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I believe he was trained to be smart, if that makes any sense, I was a PO3 in the Navy. I am an average person, but I have a great amount of book knowledge I pride myself on learning everything I can about everything, Then I went to the Navy, and they taught me all kinds of new things. I Believe BTK is smart, but not like Harvard smart, he is intelligent enough to learn, or be programmed and has the ability to handle problem solving. I have taught people to think exactly the way the Military wants them to think. Do it and don&#39;t ask questions, The tech school, he went to was militart training, and I think that is all he knows. Left brained people love writing and poetry, He has just perfected his art. and doesn&#39;t reallt think outside of the box, &#40;the obbession of his own desires.&#41;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8627-->
<!--Post: 8707--><!--Time: 1109294236-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8707"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Audreyamw<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Audreyamw<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 24, 2005 - 5:17 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->If that really was BTK, I don&#39;t think he would&#39;ve held back on the &#34;goulish details&#34; -- I think he would&#39;ve thrown a few details out for all to read, to taunt and to prove his identity -- the post just doesn&#39;t strike me as sadistic enough to actually be BTK.  Not enough &#34;chills and shivers.&#34;  YMMV. <BR> <BR>This left brain/right brain functionality is starting to intrigue me, though. I&#39;m wondering how the limited emotional capacity of psychopaths, as shown in clinical studies, has any connections to other left/right brain impediments. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8707-->
<!--Post: 8711--><!--Time: 1109294908-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8711"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Audreyamw<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Audreyamw<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 24, 2005 - 5:28 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->And who the heck goes to Hawaii for only a <i>week?</i>  Did BTK win a supermarket raffle?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8711-->
<!--Post: 8716--><!--Time: 1109295535-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8716"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Audreyamw<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Audreyamw<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 24, 2005 - 5:38 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Web resources on psychopathy and the brain: <BR> <BR>Antisocial Personality Disorder. Internet Mental Health <BR> <BR>On-Line Diagnosis of Antisocial Personality Disorder. Internet Mental Health. <BR> <BR>Dual Diagnosis and the Antisocial Personality Disorder, by Sharon C. Ekleberry, 1997. <BR> <BR>Closed head injury and frontal lobe syndrome. Brain Imaging Center, University of California at Irvine <BR> <BR>Violent tendencies linked to brain abnormality. The Chronicles. By Rob Stein &#40;Washington Post&#41;. <BR> <BR>Emotion and temperament in sociopathy. by Christopher J. Patrick. <BR> <BR>Without Conscience: Dr. Hare&#39;s Lab at the University of British Columbia <BR> <BR>Yahoo! Serial Killers Resources on the Internet <BR> <BR>Phineas Gage: 150th Anniversary Official Site <BR> <BR>The Crime Times: Research Reviews and Information on Biological Causes of Violent, Criminal and Psychopathic Behavior <BR> <BR>    <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8716-->
<!--Post: 8717--><!--Time: 1109295997-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8717"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Audreyamw<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Audreyamw<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 24, 2005 - 5:46 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text--><a href="http://www.crime-times.org/97b/w97bp4.htm" target=_top>http://www.crime-times.org/97b/w97bp4.htm</a> <BR> <BR> ...More evidence that psychopaths do not react normally to emotional stimuli comes from a new study by Rodney Day and Stephen Wong. Noting that the right hemisphere of the brain is specialized for processing the emotional significance of words, the researchers speculated that &#34;psychopaths, who are unempathic, callous, and emotionally shallow, would rely less than non- psychopaths on right-hemisphere-based decoding strategies.&#34; Instead, they theorized, psychopaths may rely more on the left hemisphere, which &#34;uses a more verbal-analytic strategy.&#34; <BR> <BR>The researchers tested 20 psychopathic penitentiary inmates, and 20 non- psychopathic inmates. Participants were shown two words—a word with negative emotional connotations, and a &#34;neutral&#34; word—in each trial. Half the time, the negative word appeared in subjects&#39; right visual field, and the neutral word in the left visual field; on the remaining trials, the order was reversed. <BR> <BR>&#34;As predicted,&#34; Day and Wong say, &#34;non-psychopaths were more accurate and faster in processing negative emotional words in the left visual field &#40;right hemisphere&#41; than in the right visual field &#40;left hemisphere&#41;. Psychopaths, on the other hand, did not show a significant visual field advantage.&#34; When negative and neutral faces were shown, however, psychopaths and non-psychopaths did not differ in their responses. This suggests, the researchers say, that the abnormal processing of emotional stimuli by psychopaths may be limited to language. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8717-->
<!--Post: 8776--><!--Time: 1109324614-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8776"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 25, 2005 - 1:43 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->All humans, even psychopaths, display psychological and behavioral trends. That&#39;s as about as specific as one can safely predict. Genuine behavioral evidence from crime scene <i>facts</i> and other <i>facts</i> can further hone a profile and this is a good thing. But problems arise from <i>interpretation</i> of these facts. <BR> <BR>For example, here are two <i>facts</i> which may or may not have been accurately interpreted. In the ONS slayings, one fact is that one attack occurred in an affluent area, and the perp did an extensive, even extrodinary amount of reconnaissance. All of this is fact. The profile states that the perp probably drives an expensive car and wears expensive clothing so he may blend in to the affluent community during his many visits. This may or may not be true, as there is no evidence of it; the only reported unusual vehicle was an old, beaten-up truck and once a Volkswagen Beetle was described. These hardly square with the profile. Another fact is that of a specific victim who was killed with blunt force trauma. This is a fact. The profile chose to label this method of murder &#34;overkill;&#34; even though the blunt force was applied <i>one</i> time. I still don&#39;t understand why one blow from a blunt object qualifies as overkill. Yet this was the profilers&#39; interpretation of a fact.  <BR> <BR>In other words, human behavior is extremely difficult to predict and even when facts are the foundation of extrapolation, the extrapolation remains subjective and inherently biased. Is ONS highly intelligent? Above average? In which category shall we place him? Like BTK, one can only look for general trends while things such as luck, timing and chance can <i>never</i> be known. <BR> <BR>Let us turn briefly to one aspect of serial killers and the study of them. If I may borrow the words of John Douglas, serial offenders, frequently, are released from prison too early because the prison shrink relies on the prisoner&#39;s &#34;self-reporting.&#34; This is true. There is additional institutional data of course, but decisions are usually made during specific sessions. What needs to be borne in mind is that the serial offenders were the ones in the first place to provide, during interviews, information to profilers! &#34;Self-reporting&#34; again. From all of this I&#39;d sum it up as &#34;look for trends, play a few hunches and pray for luck.&#34; The &#34;look for a white male in his mid 30s driving a dark blue, four-door American made vehicle at least five years old with over 100,000 miles on it&#34; stuff needs to go. Just my completely uneducated opinion. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8776-->
<!--Post: 8777--><!--Time: 1109325666-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8777"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Scbenson2001<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Scbenson2001<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 25, 2005 - 2:01 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->If I had to describe BTK in one word it would be <BR>CUNNING. I think people often mistake this for a sign of high intelligence. I have never thought BTK was anything but average intelligence wise however in his everyday life, I believe people mistake him for being slow. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8777-->
<!--Post: 9077--><!--Time: 1109392214-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9077"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Angrywolf<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Angrywolf<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 25, 2005 - 8:30 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->If it is the guy they are questioning then he has a college degree proving that he wasn&#39;t a plumber like that silly psychic said...and that he has a high level of intelligence...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9077-->
